{
  "$comment": [
    "HAND-READ, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. The 314 records no signal can join: two catalogues print two",
    "names for the same thing, and no number, carrier or corpus separates them. Somebody has to read.",
    "",
    "fr_to_en  a reading that starts from the FRENCH name and chooses the English one",
    "en_to_fr  a SECOND reading, made from the English side, without consulting the first",
    "",
    "A pair is emitted only when BOTH readings agree. This is not belt and braces: lot 98 paired the",
    "elf lineages the wrong way round and every count came back clean, because A WRONG BIJECTION IS",
    "PERFECTLY CONSISTENT. Nothing that counts can see an inversion. Two readings can.",
    "",
    "A disagreement is not an arbitration to hand to Eric -- it means one of the two readings is wrong,",
    "and it comes back in `refusals` naming both directions. A record read in one direction only is",
    "refused too: half a pairing is not a pairing.",
    "",
    "⛔ Distinct from sources/correspondence-signed.json ON PURPOSE. That file holds what ERIC signed;",
    "this one holds what an agent read. They must not be told apart by memory: the provenance on each",
    "pair says `human` for his and `reading/two-way` for these.",
    "",
    "See docs/CORRESPONDENCE.md."
  ],
